From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Barnes <hello@jonbarnes.dev>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 18:20:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] The alpha test runs on foliage too

Patch 0013 of the renderer series (OoT: Recompiled).

Patch 0012 left this game's foliage lit correctly and casting nothing, with one artifact: where a
quad crossed something lit differently, its rectangle showed. The cause is one early return.

alphaCoverage answers "fully covered" for any draw that declares neither an alpha compare nor the
coverage cut, and this game's foliage in the translucent z mode declares neither. So its
transparent texels have always counted as surface to every ray. That is the quad shaped shadow,
the transparent outline that casts it, and the cut-outs, from one cause.

An earlier attempt at this problem removed the cut-out depth compare instead, on the reading that
this alpha test already covered these draws. It does not, and taking the compare away left
nothing dropping them at all, which was worse. Reverted, and the reasoning kept here so the same
reading is not made a third time.

A threshold has to be chosen, which is why this arrives on the Experiment row rather than simply
on. With no compare declared the threshold lands at zero, and a test against zero passes every
texel, so turning the test on without choosing one would change nothing. An eighth is the cut the
coverage rule already uses for this game's own edge textures; a half is offered beside it.

Rung 17 is rung 16 with the test on and the shadow still off, so the test can be judged alone.
Rung 18 puts the shadow back, which is the point: a leaf tested at the hit casts a leaf rather
than the quad it is drawn on. Rung 19 is rung 18 at the stricter cut.

A draw that declares its own compare is untouched: the chosen cut is taken as a maximum beside it.

With the ray tracing row Off none of this runs.
---
diff --git a/src/shaders/Raytracing.hlsl b/src/shaders/Raytracing.hlsl
--- a/src/shaders/Raytracing.hlsl
+++ b/src/shaders/Raytracing.hlsl
@@ -1298,7 +1298,27 @@ float alphaCoverage(uint instanceId, uint primitiveIndex, float2 barycentrics, b
     // only and so never ran on them ("fences ladders, vines etc still not working", the user,
     // 2026-09-24).
     const bool coverageCut = otherMode.cvgXAlpha();
-    if ((alphaCompare != G_AC_THRESHOLD) && (alphaCompare != G_AC_DITHER) && !coverageCut) {
+    // THE FOLIAGE THIS GAME DECLARES NOTHING ABOUT (patch 0013). The draws the cut-out rules
+    // reclassify as solid, which is this game's trees and leaf clumps, sit in the translucent z
+    // mode and never write depth, and they use NEITHER alpha compare NOR the coverage cut. So
+    // every test above passes them straight through as "fully covered", their transparent texels
+    // included, and every ray treats the whole quad as surface. That is the quad shaped shadow,
+    // the transparent outline that casts it, and the cut-outs where a quad crosses something lit
+    // differently: one cause, three symptoms, reported on 2026-09-30 as all three.
+    //
+    // WHY THE EARLIER ATTEMPT AT THIS WAS WRONG, since the reverted patch is worth learning from:
+    // it assumed this test already ran on these draws and removed the depth compare that was the
+    // only thing dropping them. Reading the any-hit shader showed an alpha test; what it did not
+    // show was the early return above, which excludes the very class being reasoned about.
+    //
+    // A THRESHOLD HAS TO BE CHOSEN, and that is why this is on a rung rather than simply on. With
+    // no compare declared the threshold below lands at zero, and a test against zero passes every
+    // texel, so turning the test on alone would change nothing at all. An eighth is the same cut
+    // the coverage rule uses for the game's own edge textures; a half is offered beside it for a
+    // texture whose transparent regions are not fully transparent.
+    const bool reclassifiedFoliage = (RtParams.tuneExperiment.x >= 17.0f) &&
+                                     (otherMode.zMode() == ZMODE_XLU) && !otherMode.zUpd();
+    if ((alphaCompare != G_AC_THRESHOLD) && (alphaCompare != G_AC_DITHER) && !coverageCut && !reclassifiedFoliage) {
         return 1.0f;
     }
     if (!renderFlagUsesTexture0(rp.flags)) {
@@ -1346,6 +1366,12 @@ float alphaCoverage(uint instanceId, uint primitiveIndex, float2 barycentrics, b
     // compare (random per pixel on the console), and an eighth for the coverage cut; a draw
     // with both takes the higher.
     float threshold = coverageCut ? 0.125f : 0.0f;
+    // The chosen cut for a draw that declares none (patch 0013): an eighth, or a half on the rung
+    // that asks for it. Taken as a maximum like every other, so a draw that DOES declare a compare
+    // keeps its own and is unaffected by any of this.
+    if (reclassifiedFoliage) {
+        threshold = max(threshold, (RtParams.tuneExperiment.x >= 19.0f) ? 0.5f : 0.125f);
+    }
     if (alphaCompare == G_AC_THRESHOLD) {
         threshold = max(threshold, instanceRDPParams[ri.instanceIndex].blendColor.a);
     }
diff --git a/src/render/rt64_framebuffer_renderer.cpp b/src/render/rt64_framebuffer_renderer.cpp
--- a/src/render/rt64_framebuffer_renderer.cpp
+++ b/src/render/rt64_framebuffer_renderer.cpp
@@ -1869,6 +1869,16 @@ namespace RT64 {
                             case 14: solidDraw = otherMode.zCmp(); castsNothing = true; break;
                             case 15: solidDraw = otherMode.zCmp() && manyTriangles; break;
                             case 16: solidDraw = otherMode.zCmp() && manyTriangles; castsNothing = true; break;
+                            // 17 to 19 are rung 16 with the alpha test at the hit turned on for
+                            // these draws (patch 0013, in alphaCoverage). 17 keeps the shadow off
+                            // so the test can be judged on its own; 18 puts the shadow BACK, which
+                            // is the point of the whole exercise, because a leaf that is tested at
+                            // the hit casts a leaf rather than the quad it is drawn on; 19 is 18
+                            // with a stricter cut for a texture whose transparent parts are not
+                            // quite transparent.
+                            case 17: solidDraw = otherMode.zCmp() && manyTriangles; castsNothing = true; break;
+                            case 18: solidDraw = otherMode.zCmp() && manyTriangles; break;
+                            case 19: solidDraw = otherMode.zCmp() && manyTriangles; break;
                             default: solidDraw = otherMode.cvgXAlpha() || (acMode == G_AC_THRESHOLD) || (acMode == G_AC_DITHER); break;
                         }
                         // A translucent draw (the XLU z mode) gets a mask no ray carries (patch 0006).
